{# The phone navigation drawer.

   Seven entries make a thousand pixels of links for a row that offers three
   hundred and fifty-nine: below `md` the bar wrapped onto two rows and took
   one hundred and thirty-seven pixels before the page started, and the first
   page added by a client would have made it three. So the entries go behind
   a button, and the bar falls back to one row.

   `<details>` rather than a checkbox or a button: the browser provides
   opening, closing, the keyboard and the state announced to screen readers,
   and the drawer works before a line of JavaScript arrives.
   `data-dropdown` adds Escape to it (`shared/utils/detailsDropdown.js`), and
   the backdrop is closed by `shared/utils/navDrawer.js`. Without either, the
   button that opened the drawer closes it: it stays above the backdrop and
   shows a cross while the panel is there.

   The panel is `fixed`, and that is why the header no longer carries its blur
   itself: `backdrop-filter` makes its element the containing block of its
   fixed descendants, and `inset-y-0` stopped at the bar's one hundred and
   thirty-seven pixels instead of filling the screen height. See
   `layout.html.twig`.

   Expects: `primaryMenu`, `accountMenu`. #}
<details class="group md:hidden" data-dropdown data-nav-drawer>
    <summary class="relative z-50 flex cursor-pointer list-none select-none items-center rounded-md p-2 text-secondary transition-colors hover:bg-surface-2/60 hover:text-primary [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <span class="sr-only">{{ 'shared.main_menu'|trans }}</span>
        {{ include('@Shared/components/icon.html.twig', {name: 'menu', class: 'w-6 h-6 group-open:hidden', size: 24}) }}
        {{ include('@Shared/components/icon.html.twig', {name: 'x', class: 'w-6 h-6 hidden group-open:block', size: 24}) }}
    </summary>

    <div data-nav-drawer-veil class="fixed inset-0 z-30 bg-black/40" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <nav
        class="fixed inset-y-0 right-0 z-40 flex w-[min(19rem,85vw)] flex-col gap-2 overflow-y-auto border-l border-line bg-bg p-2 pt-16 text-sm"
        aria-label="{{ 'shared.main_menu'|trans }}"
    >
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-0.5">
            {{ include('Frontend/themes/default/partials/menu_mobile.html.twig', {items: primaryMenu}) }}
        </div>

        {# The account is not a page of the site, it is a service door: it
           sits at the bottom, behind a rule, rather than among the
           sections. #}
        {% if accountMenu is not empty %}
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-col gap-0.5 border-t border-line pt-2">
                {{ include('Frontend/themes/default/partials/menu_mobile.html.twig', {items: accountMenu}) }}
            </div>
        {% endif %}
    </nav>
</details>
